(Regular file exact fit: a fixed buffer that fills exactly at EOF must not signal a spurious overflow error.)

(Create a 10-byte regular file.)
open a file for writing called w at "./b341_data.txt".
Write "0123456789" to w.
Close w.

(A 10-byte fixed buffer reading a 10-byte file fills exactly at EOF.)
a buffer called buf is 10 bytes in size.
open a file for reading called f at "./b341_data.txt".
Read from f into buf.
On error print "ERROR: false overflow on exact fit".
Print "bytes: ".
Print buf.
Print "length: ".
Print buf's size.
Close f.
Delete the file "./b341_data.txt".